---
/**
 * Privacy Policy — written for India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023
 * (DPDP Act) and the Information Technology Act, 2000 and its rules.
 * Keep this in sync with what the website actually does: if analytics, cookies,
 * embeds or a form provider are added, update sections 3, 4, 6 and 7.
 */
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const updated = "7 October 2026";
const sections = [
  { id: "who-we-are", title: "Who we are" },
  { id: "scope", title: "What this policy covers" },
  { id: "data-we-collect", title: "Personal data we collect" },
  { id: "how-we-use", title: "How we use it and why" },
  { id: "cookies", title: "Cookies and tracking" },
  { id: "sharing", title: "Who we share it with" },
  { id: "transfers", title: "Where data is stored" },
  { id: "retention", title: "How long we keep it" },
  { id: "security", title: "Security" },
  { id: "your-rights", title: "Your rights" },
  { id: "children", title: "Children" },
  { id: "products", title: "Our products" },
  { id: "changes", title: "Changes to this policy" },
  { id: "grievance", title: "Contact and grievance officer" },
];
const mail = `mailto:${site.email}`;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Reofex Technologies collects, uses and protects personal data on reofex.com and in business enquiries, under India's DPDP Act 2023."
  updated={updated}
  intro="We collect as little personal data as we can, use it only to respond to you and work with you, and never sell it."
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="who-we-are">
    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This website is operated by <strong>Reofex Technologies</strong> ("Reofex", "we", "us", "our"), a software company
      based in India that builds SaaS products, AI and automation solutions and custom software.
    </p>
    <p>
      For personal data collected through this website and through enquiries you send us, Reofex is the{" "}
      <strong>Data Fiduciary</strong> under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 ("DPDP Act"): we decide why
      and how that data is processed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="scope">
    <h2>2. What this policy covers</h2>
    <p>This policy applies to personal data we process when you:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>visit this website;</li>
      <li>contact us through the contact form, by email, on WhatsApp or through our social media profiles;</li>
      <li>discuss, request or receive a proposal for our services or products.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Data you or your organisation put into one of our products is covered by that product's own terms and privacy
      policy — see <a href="#products">section 12</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="data-we-collect">
    <h2>3. Personal data we collect</h2>
    <h3>Information you give us</h3>
    <div class="lg__table">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">What we receive</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Contact form</td>
            <td>Your name, email address, company (optional), the topic you select and your message.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Email</td>
            <td>Your email address, name and anything you include in the message or its attachments.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>WhatsApp ("Get Started")</td>
            <td>
              If you choose to message us on WhatsApp, we receive your WhatsApp phone number, profile name and the messages
              you send.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Business discussions</td>
            <td>Contact details and business information you share with us while we scope or deliver work.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Please don't send us sensitive personal data (such as financial, health or government ID information) or
      confidential business information through the contact form or WhatsApp. If a project requires it, we'll agree a
      secure method with you first.
    </p>
    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
    <p>
      Like any website, the servers that deliver this site record standard technical information when pages are
      requested — such as IP address, browser type, the page requested and the date and time. This is used only to
      deliver the website, keep it secure and diagnose problems.
    </p>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> use analytics, advertising pixels, session recording or fingerprinting on this website.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="how-we-use">
    <h2>4. How we use it and why</h2>
    <p>We process personal data only for the purposes below:</p>
    <div class="lg__table">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Basis under the DPDP Act</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Replying to your enquiry and continuing the conversation you started</td>
            <td>Your consent, given when you contact us, or a use you voluntarily provided the data for</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Preparing proposals and providing services you request</td>
            <td>Your consent / steps you ask us to take</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Operating, securing and troubleshooting the website</td>
            <td>Legitimate uses permitted under the DPDP Act</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Meeting legal, tax and accounting obligations, and responding to lawful requests</td>
            <td>Compliance with law</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> sell personal data, use it for third-party advertising, or add you to marketing lists
      without asking. If we'd like to send you updates in future, we'll ask for your consent separately, and you can
      withdraw it at any time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="cookies">
    <h2>5. Cookies and tracking</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not set cookies and does not use analytics or advertising trackers. Our fonts and images are
      served from our own website, not from third-party services.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you use the footer's "Start a conversation" field, your email address is kept temporarily in your browser's
      session storage so it can be filled into the contact form. It is not sent to us until you submit the form, and it's
      cleared once the contact page reads it or when you close the tab.
    </p>
    <p>If we ever introduce cookies or analytics, we will update this policy and ask for consent where required.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing">
    <h2>6. Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We share personal data only where needed for the purposes above, with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Service providers</strong> that help us run our business — such as website hosting, email and, if
        enabled, a form-delivery service. They process data on our instructions and under confidentiality obligations.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Meta Platforms (WhatsApp)</strong>, when you choose to message us on WhatsApp. WhatsApp's own terms and
        privacy policy apply to your use of WhatsApp.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Professional advisers</strong> (such as lawyers and accountants) where necessary.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Authorities</strong>, where we are required to by law, court order or lawful request, or to protect our
        rights, users or the public.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A successor business</strong>, if Reofex is involved in a merger, acquisition or sale of assets — in which
        case this policy will continue to apply to your data.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Links on this website to our product sites, social media profiles (LinkedIn, Instagram, GitHub) and other third
      parties are governed by those parties' own privacy policies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="transfers">
    <h2>7. Where data is stored</h2>
    <p>
      Some of our service providers may store or process data outside India. Where this happens, we transfer data only
      as permitted under the DPDP Act, including any restrictions notified by the Government of India, and we take
      reasonable steps to ensure it remains protected.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention">
    <h2>8. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep personal data only for as long as it's needed for the purpose it was collected for — for example, for the
      duration of an enquiry and any resulting business relationship — and then delete it, unless we need to keep it
      longer to meet legal, tax or accounting requirements or to resolve disputes.
    </p>
    <p>
      If an enquiry doesn't lead to further contact, we periodically delete it. You can ask us to delete your data
      sooner at any time (see <a href="#your-rights">section 10</a>).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="security">
    <h2>9. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable security safeguards to protect personal data against unauthorised access, loss, misuse or
      alteration, including encrypted connections (HTTPS) and restricted access to the systems that hold enquiries. No
      method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but we work to protect your data and will notify you and
      the Data Protection Board of India of a personal data breach where the law requires us to.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-rights">
    <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the DPDP Act, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> a summary of the personal data we hold about you and how we process it;</li>
      <li><strong>Correct, complete or update</strong> inaccurate or incomplete data;</li>
      <li><strong>Erase</strong> your data where it's no longer needed or you withdraw consent, unless the law requires us to keep it;</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time — this won't affect processing that already took place;</li>
      <li><strong>Grievance redressal</strong> — to raise a complaint with us about how your data is handled;</li>
      <li><strong>Nominate</strong> another person to exercise these rights on your behalf in the event of death or incapacity.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, email <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a>. We may need to verify your identity before
      acting on a request. If you're not satisfied with our response, you may complain to the{" "}
      <strong>Data Protection Board of India</strong>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="children">
    <h2>11. Children</h2>
    <p>
      This website and our services are intended for businesses and are not directed at anyone under 18. We do not
      knowingly collect personal data from children. If you believe a child has sent us personal data, please contact us
      and we will delete it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="products">
    <h2>12. Our products</h2>
    <p>
      Our products — <a href="/products/respondly">Respondly</a>, <a href="/products/reofex-growth">Reofex Growth</a>,{" "}
      <a href="/products/reofex-sync">Reofex Sync</a> and <a href="/products/fynex">Fynex</a> — have their own terms and
      privacy information, which apply when you use them.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a business uses our products to process its own customers' or employees' data, that business is the Data
      Fiduciary and Reofex processes the data on its behalf and on its instructions. Fynex is self-hosted: it runs on the
      customer's own infrastructure, and the customer controls that data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as our website, products or the law change. The "Last updated" date at the top shows
      when it was last revised. If we make significant changes, we'll make that clear on this page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="grievance">
    <h2>14. Contact and grievance officer</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about this policy, to exercise your rights or to raise a grievance, contact our Grievance Officer:
    </p>
    <p class="lg__note">
      <strong>Grievance Officer, Reofex Technologies</strong><br />
      Email: <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      We will acknowledge your grievance promptly and aim to resolve it within 30 days, or within any shorter period
      required by law.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
